{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Flock by flock alone.</b> So that it be seen that in every kind there is a number of males and females as is fitting for the task of livestock, so that they can be fruitful and multiply, as he says: קַח נָא אֶת בִּרְכָתִי (Genesis 33:11) — for it was a gift prepared for blessing, which is the addition of good." "<b>And you shall put a space between flock and flock.</b> Lest the animals rush from flock to flock and intermingle, and the observer not discern the wisdom of the gift and its blessing."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:58.877928931Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}